<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">National League for Democracy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1988">1988</a>–<a href="/years/2023">2023</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as NLD</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National League for Democracy is a political party of Myanmar founded in 1988 after the pro-democracy uprising, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aung-san-suu-kyi">Aung San Suu Kyi</a>. It won the 1990 election, which the military ignored, and the elections of 2015 and 2020. Its government was overthrown by the coup of February 2021, and the junta dissolved it in 2023.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/national-league-for-democracy.jpg" alt="National League for Democracy" width="320" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: National League for Democracy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_National_League_for_Democracy.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
